{{fbdoc item="title" value="SpiderMonkey"}}----
Embeddable JavaScript engine.

Website: [[https://www-archive.mozilla.org/js/spidermonkey/]]
Source: [[https://archive.mozilla.org/pub/js/js-1.60.tar.gz|Mozilla SpiderMonkey 1.6 archive]]
Platforms supported: ""Win32"", Linux
Headers to include: spidermonkey/jsapi.bi
Header version: SpiderMonkey 1.6

{{fbdoc item="section" value="Native SDK and values"}}
	Use the archived 1.6 C embedding API with these examples. Current SpiderMonkey SDKs have a different embedding API. The native Win32 build uses 32-bit ##JSWord## and ##jsval## values; its DLL and import library belong to a Win32 application. The SDK's CPU configuration cannot be carried unchanged into a Win64 build.

	C ##int##, ##JSBool##, ##int32## and ##uint32## use 32-bit types. The low three bits of a ##jsval## encode its type. Use the binding's conversion macros rather than dereferencing a tagged value directly. ##JS_TRUE## and ##JS_FALSE## use C's 1 and 0 boolean representation, including when encoded by ##BOOLEAN_TO_JSVAL##.

	The actual Win32 SDK from Mozilla's ##js-1.60.tar.gz## archive has been checked with independent C layouts, both FreeBASIC backends, native callbacks, GC roots and all three examples. The same archived engine also passes on Linux i386 with both backends, C layouts, callbacks, GC roots and all three examples. On Linux amd64 use a 32-bit executable and matching runtime; native Win64 execution remains separate. Generate jsautocfg.h using the actual i386 CPU-configuration program. Apply ##build_scripts/patches/spidermonkey16-fdlibm-errno.patch## privately: the global-errno workaround belongs to ##XP_WIN##, while Unix must use ##<errno.h>## to match glibc thread-local errno. The patch preserves the Windows workaround. The SDK was built without ##JS_THREADSAFE##, so one application thread owns each runtime and its contexts.

{{fbdoc item="section" value="Ownership and cleanup"}}
	Check every runtime, context, object, string and function creation result. ##JSClass## is borrowed by its objects and must remain valid for their lifetime. Destroy contexts before their runtime, and call ##JS_ShutDown()## after the application has finished with all SpiderMonkey runtimes.

	##JS_GetStringBytes()## returns borrowed storage. Copy it before keeping it across an API call which may allocate or collect. ##JS_NewStringCopyN()## copies a caller's buffer into SDK-owned storage. ##JS_NewString()## instead accepts an owned buffer obtained through ##JS_malloc()##; an ordinary FreeBASIC string buffer must not be passed to it.

	Protect a ##jsval## held outside the engine with ##JS_AddRoot(cx, @value)## before a possible garbage collection, then remove that root with ##JS_RemoveRoot(cx, @value)## before the context is destroyed. The root tracks the value's storage address, so keep that address valid. Native callbacks return ##JS_TRUE## on success, set their result through ##rval##, and return ##JS_FALSE## on failure.

{{fbdoc item="ex"}}
{{fbdoc item="filename" value="examples/manual/libraries/spidermonkey1.bas"}}%%(freebasic)
'' examples/manual/libraries/spidermonkey1.bas
''
'' Example extracted from the FreeBASIC Manual
'' from topic 'SpiderMonkey'
'' Purpose: Evaluate JavaScript using the archived SpiderMonkey 1.6 API.
'' Responsibilities: Checked engine setup, borrowed strings and owned cleanup.
'' This example contains no JavaScript engine implementation or worker threads.
''
'' See Also: https://www.freebasic.net/wiki/wikka.php?wakka=ExtLibspidermonkey
'' --------

'' Evaluating javascript code
#include Once "spidermonkey/jsapi.bi"

' The SDK borrows this class descriptor for every object's lifetime.
' A single application thread owns the runtime and its callbacks.
Dim Shared As JSClass global_class = _
( _
	@"global", 0, _
	@JS_PropertyStub, @JS_PropertyStub, @JS_PropertyStub, @JS_PropertyStub, _
	@JS_EnumerateStub, @JS_ResolveStub, @JS_ConvertStub, @JS_FinalizeStub _
)

Const TEST_SCRIPT = _
	!"function fact(n)           \n" + _
	!"{                          \n" + _
	!"    if (n <= 1)            \n" + _
	!"        return 1;          \n" + _
	!"                           \n" + _
	!"    return n * fact(n - 1);\n" + _
	!"}                          \n" + _
	!"                           \n" + _
	!"    fact(5)                \n"

Function run_example() As Integer
	Dim As JSRuntime Ptr rt
	Dim As JSContext Ptr cx
	Dim As Integer status = 1
	Do
		' One MiB GC budget; 4096 selects the context's stack chunk size.
		rt = JS_NewRuntime(1048576)
		If rt = 0 Then Exit Do
		cx = JS_NewContext(rt, 4096)
		If cx = 0 Then Exit Do
		Dim As JSObject Ptr global = JS_NewObject(cx, @global_class, NULL, NULL)
		If global = 0 Then Exit Do
		JS_SetGlobalObject(cx, global)
		If JS_InitStandardClasses(cx, global) = 0 Then Exit Do
		Dim As jsval rval
		If JS_EvaluateScript(cx, global, TEST_SCRIPT, Len(TEST_SCRIPT), "localhost", 1, @rval) = 0 Then Exit Do
		Dim As JSString Ptr result_string = JS_ValueToString(cx, rval)
		If result_string = 0 Then Exit Do
		Dim As ZString Ptr result_bytes = JS_GetStringBytes(result_string)
		If result_bytes = 0 Then Exit Do
		Print "result: " & *result_bytes
		status = 0
	Loop While 0
	' Destroy contexts before their runtime, then release process-wide state.
	If cx <> 0 Then JS_DestroyContext(cx)
	If rt <> 0 Then JS_DestroyRuntime(rt)
	JS_ShutDown()
	Return status
End Function

Dim As Integer status = run_example()
If status <> 0 Then Print "SpiderMonkey example failed"
End status
'' end of spidermonkey1.bas
%%

{{fbdoc item="filename" value="examples/manual/libraries/spidermonkey2.bas"}}%%(freebasic)
'' examples/manual/libraries/spidermonkey2.bas
''
'' Example extracted from the FreeBASIC Manual
'' from topic 'SpiderMonkey'
'' Purpose: Evaluate JavaScript using the archived SpiderMonkey 1.6 API.
'' Responsibilities: Checked engine setup, borrowed strings and owned cleanup.
'' This example contains no JavaScript engine implementation or worker threads.
''
'' See Also: https://www.freebasic.net/wiki/wikka.php?wakka=ExtLibspidermonkey
'' --------

'' Callback example: Functions that are used by the Javascript code,
'' but are implemented in FB.
#include Once "spidermonkey/jsapi.bi"

' The SDK borrows this class descriptor for every object's lifetime.
' A single application thread owns the runtime and its callbacks.
Dim Shared As JSClass global_class = _
( _
	@"global", 0, _
	@JS_PropertyStub, @JS_PropertyStub, @JS_PropertyStub, @JS_PropertyStub, _
	@JS_EnumerateStub, @JS_ResolveStub, @JS_ConvertStub, @JS_FinalizeStub _
)

Private Function print_callback cdecl _
	( _
		ByVal cx As JSContext Ptr, _
		ByVal obj As JSObject Ptr, _
		ByVal argc As uintN, _
		ByVal argv As jsval Ptr, _
		ByVal rval As jsval Ptr _
	) As JSBool

	If (argc < 1 OrElse argv = 0 OrElse rval = 0) Then
		Return 0
	End If

	Dim As JSString Ptr arg_string = JS_ValueToString(cx, argv[0])
	If arg_string = 0 Then Return 0
	Dim As ZString Ptr arg_bytes = JS_GetStringBytes(arg_string)
	If arg_bytes = 0 Then Return 0
	Print *arg_bytes
	*rval = JSVAL_VOID
	Return 1
End Function

Private Function ucase_callback cdecl _
	( _
		ByVal cx As JSContext Ptr, _
		ByVal obj As JSObject Ptr, _
		ByVal argc As uintN, _
		ByVal argv As jsval Ptr, _
		ByVal rval As jsval Ptr _
	) As JSBool

	If (argc < 1 OrElse argv = 0 OrElse rval = 0) Then
		Return 0
	End If

	Dim As JSString Ptr arg_string = JS_ValueToString(cx, argv[0])
	If arg_string = 0 Then Return 0
	Dim As ZString Ptr arg_bytes = JS_GetStringBytes(arg_string)
	If arg_bytes = 0 Then Return 0
	' Copy borrowed bytes before calling an API which can allocate or collect.
	Dim As String result = UCase(*arg_bytes)
	Dim As JSString Ptr result_string = JS_NewStringCopyN(cx, StrPtr(result), Len(result))
	If result_string = 0 Then Return 0
	' The SDK owns the copy; the FreeBASIC string can leave scope safely.
	*rval = STRING_TO_JSVAL(result_string)
	Return 1
End Function

Const TEST_SCRIPT = "print(ucase('hello'));"

Function run_example() As Integer
	Dim As JSRuntime Ptr rt
	Dim As JSContext Ptr cx
	Dim As Integer status = 1
	Do
		' One MiB GC budget; 4096 selects the context's stack chunk size.
		rt = JS_NewRuntime(1048576)
		If rt = 0 Then Exit Do
		cx = JS_NewContext(rt, 4096)
		If cx = 0 Then Exit Do
		Dim As JSObject Ptr global = JS_NewObject(cx, @global_class, NULL, NULL)
		If global = 0 Then Exit Do
		JS_SetGlobalObject(cx, global)
		If JS_InitStandardClasses(cx, global) = 0 Then Exit Do
		If JS_DefineFunction(cx, global, "print", @print_callback, 1, 0) = 0 Then Exit Do
		If JS_DefineFunction(cx, global, "ucase", @ucase_callback, 1, 0) = 0 Then Exit Do
		Dim As jsval rval
		If JS_EvaluateScript(cx, global, TEST_SCRIPT, Len(TEST_SCRIPT), "localhost", 1, @rval) = 0 Then Exit Do
		status = 0
	Loop While 0
	' Destroy contexts before their runtime, then release process-wide state.
	If cx <> 0 Then JS_DestroyContext(cx)
	If rt <> 0 Then JS_DestroyRuntime(rt)
	JS_ShutDown()
	Return status
End Function

Dim As Integer status = run_example()
If status <> 0 Then Print "SpiderMonkey example failed"
End status
'' end of spidermonkey2.bas
%%

